==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|senile|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|senilis|senīlis|of or pertaining to old age|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|senex||old|lang=la}}, from Gaulish and {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{recons|sénos||old|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, or relating to [[old age]].
# {{context|often|offensive}} [[exhibit|Exhibiting]] the [[deterioration]] in [[mind]] and [[body]] often [[accompanying]] old age; [[doddering]].

